    "narrative": "For the May 6th slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **James Wood** (73.62) anchor our offensive effort as our highest-projected starters. **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime spot against Freddy Peralta; despite the pitcher's talent, the combination of a high-ceiling hitter\u2019s park and an elite platoon advantage (+14%) drives his valuation, with his aggressive base-stealing potential enhanced by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery. Similarly, **James Wood** earns his high floor by leading off against an approachable matchup, allowing him to maximize his opportunities to accumulate volume stats. **Trevor Story** (66.34) and **Brice Turang** (66.93) also present strong value, with **Trevor Story** benefiting from favorable wind conditions and **Brice Turang** serving as a dual-threat asset against Pallante thanks to the potential for stolen bases against a slow-working battery.\n\nStrategic considerations for today forced some difficult decisions, particularly concerning our bench depth. **Kyle Karros** (48.55) was our closest call, nearly breaking into the lineup due to the park factors in Milwaukee, but he ultimately remained benched because his efficiency metrics didn't quite eclipse the high-floor production of our current outfield and utility options. We are also monitoring **Jose Caballero**, who missed the cut not just for failing to meet our 40.0 efficiency threshold, but due to a 45% rain risk hanging over his contest against Eovaldi. On the other end of the spectrum, we are wary of the heavy lift required by **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**, both of whom are facing the elite arm of Paul Skenes. While **Corbin Carroll** maintains a \"Strong\" 59.90 score due to his high base projection, his performance will be the primary bellwether for our success against a top-tier pitcher today.",
